# APIs and Integrations

- Inspect existing API conventions before adding endpoints.
- Define request/response contracts, validation, errors, auth and versioning expectations.
- Use timeouts, bounded retries with backoff, idempotency where needed, and clear failure handling.
- Do not retry non-idempotent operations blindly.
- Keep credentials server-side and use environment/configuration patterns already present.
- Validate webhook signatures when supported; protect against replay and duplicate delivery.
- Document external dependencies, quotas, rate limits and degraded-mode behavior.
